s kingside castling\n- Keeps options open for various pawn structures\n- Follows classical opening principles (knights before bishops)\n\nReason: Nf3 is the strongest move because it develops a piece with tempo (controlling the center), prepares castling, and maintains maximum flexibility. It's a fundamental principle to develop knights before bishops in the opening, and Nf3 is the most flexible square for the knight, controlling e5 and d4 while supporting future central pawn breaks.\n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
