iative\n\n**Reason:**\n\nI'm choosing N: d4-c6 because it delivers check to the Black king on e8. This forcing move gives me several advantages:\n1. It forces Black to respond to the check immediately\n2. It keeps Black's king in the center, preventing castling\n3. The knight on c6 will be excellently placed, controlling key central squares\n4. It maintains my initiative and puts pressure on Black's uncoordinated position\n\nThis is superior to quiet developing moves because in this tactical position, keeping the opponent's king exposed is paramount.\n\n**Answer: N: d4-c6**"}
